@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# Trace: string input throws `RangeError`, not `CsvError`
+
+## README line violated
+
+> For every string `text`, `parseCsvLine` either returns the fields as an array
+> of strings, or throws `CsvError` (exported, a subclass of `Error`). It never
+> throws anything else, never hangs, ...
+
+(and, from the intro: "the input is anything at all").
+
+## Input
+
+A record consisting of `2 ** 27` (134 217 728) commas and nothing else, i.e.
+128 MiB of `,`. It is a valid record of 134 217 729 empty fields.
+
+```js
+const text = ",".repeat(2 ** 27);
+```
+
+One comma fewer (`",".repeat(2 ** 27 - 1)`) returns an array of length
+134 217 728 as expected; from `2 ** 27` commas upward the parser throws.
+
+## Command (from the project root)
+
+```sh
+node --input-type=module -e 'import * as csv from "./src/csv.mjs"; const text = ",".repeat(2 ** 27); Promise.resolve().then(() => csv.parseCsvLine(text)).then((r) => console.log("returned array of length", r.length), (e) => console.log("threw:", e.constructor.name, "| instanceof CsvError:", e instanceof csv.CsvError, "| instanceof Error:", e instanceof Error, "|", e.message));'
+```
+
+Default node settings, no heap flags (node v25.2.1, macOS arm64). Needs about
+3 GB of RAM and finishes in 2-3 s.
+
+## Expected
+
+Either `returned array of length 134217729` (an array of 134 217 729 empty
+strings) or `threw: CsvError ...`. Nothing else is allowed by the contract.
+
+## Actual
+
+```
+threw: RangeError | instanceof CsvError: false | instanceof Error: true | Invalid array length
+```
+
+`parseCsvLine` throws a `RangeError` (V8's per-array element limit is hit by
+`fields.push("")` in the `FIELD_START` branch of `src/csv.mjs`). The error is
+not a `CsvError`, so a caller that does `catch (e) { if (e instanceof CsvError) ... }`
+lets it escape. Same result observed for 200 MB of commas
+(`",".repeat(209715200)`), with and without `--max-old-space-size=8192`.
+
+## Notes
+
+- It is not an out-of-memory crash: the process stays alive, the throw is an
+  ordinary catchable exception, and RSS stays around 2-3.6 GB.
+- The threshold is exactly the number of fields (134 217 729 = 2^27 + 1), not
+  the byte size: 200 MB of `"a",` (52 428 801 fields) parses fine in ~1.7 s.
